-- why NAME, unexplained [FILE ...] (“The Hyperactive Workflow”: every declaration is there for a
-- reason, a chain to a root of the workflow): a node of the graph is a part of a node with a reason,
-- or a root; a declaration whose statement says (part of NODE) or (prerequisite to NODE) has NODE's
-- reason; a name the machine itself names (a string of src/) has the machine as its reason; and what
-- a declaration with a reason uses has that reason too. The nodes come from the views kept in the
-- store, the uses from the checker's record (deps/, users/), the statements from the written pieces.
hy-node-table : List (List Word) → List (List Word × List (List Word))
hy-node-table nil = nil
hy-node-table (cons l r) = cons (hy-head (h-split #32 l) , h-tail-lists (h-split #32 l)) (hy-node-table r)
